## M1 - supported reader forms: accept safeguard; qualify diagnosis
The old member regex is zero-prefix-only, but 0124.prime-desk DOES match it.
Thus the regex alone does not reject every new zero-prefix return line. The real
compatibility boundary also includes legacy member directory and receipt/payload
schema assumptions. Nonzero members, page-local N7NN tails and new matching-line
custody must each have an explicit supported reader or visible unsupported state.
The prime_support folder scan recognizes 05.NN.md, so exact N7NN references need
an explicit route; it must not silently hide them. Unsupported inputs may appear
as clearly explained unprojected records; the problem is silence or false complete
coverage, not the word unprojected. Correct this overstatement in the test oracle
interpretation without overwriting Claude's original text or cases.

## M2 - avoid a second status authority: accept with limit
Reusing desk_state formatting is useful. Its fixture record is not an automatic
new authority over live assignments or reviews. However, a clearly derived,
source-bound cache/projection is permissible; storing a view is not by itself
an authority violation. First slice remains read-only. The catalog indexes exact
sources/attributed supplied labels; no duplicated status engine or shadow task text.

## M3 - parallel work: accept minimum, no schema expansion now
The canonical selector owns one primary work item. Parallel references may be
listed explicitly by the catalog with supplied/index basis and their source
links. Claim/return observations come from actual pages; observed bytes do not
authenticate release or prove a currently running process. Do not infer availability
from silence. No selector schema revision or new authority is necessary now.
These safeguards are already in 0420 and 0524/05.01. Do not interrupt the active
builder or silently change its frozen pack; test the return against them.

## Oracle corrections and first-use limits
C04: distinguish review completed, custody complete, disposition and Director
approval. The forbidden shorthand reviewed means accepted should not ban showing
an explicitly supplied, properly attributed technical acceptance disposition.
C11's absence is a property of the deliberately bounded fixture, not a claim that
the historical file is missing from the actual workspace.
C16 names expected N7NN tails not all present in its frozen sources. Treat it as
a declarative constructed fixture, not a fully sourced real-frozen observation.
C17's line 0124.prime-desk matches the old regex; test actual schema/reader limits
and a nonzero prefix. Exact source bytes are preserved in packet/drill-down; the
short overview may quote a bounded excerpt if it clearly links the complete text.
Don't require dumping every Director sentence or historic encoding fault into the
short view. Unresolved holds and known limitations remain visible.
The checker is a small in-lab shape checker, not a robust general schema validator
or executable 18-case tool harness. The cases require independent application
against the returned desk tool before behavior can be claimed.

## First-use plan and disposition
0521/05.03 is a useful rehearsal: reviewed material with pending custody and a
